      "text": "To solve the problem, we start with the given equation:\n\n\\[x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0.\\]\n\nThis can be rearranged to:\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the sum:\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1.\\]\n\nNotice that this sum is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = x\\) and common ratio \\(r = x\\), and it has 2017 terms. The sum \\(S\\) of the first 2017 terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[S = \\frac{x(1 - x^{2017})}{1 - x}.\\]\n\nFrom the given equation, we know that \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Substituting this into the sum formula, we get:\n\n\\[S = \\frac{x(1 - (2x - 1))}{1 - x} = \\frac{x(1 - 2x + 1)}{1 - x} = \\frac{x(2 - 2x)}{1 - x} = \\frac{2x(1 - x)}{1 - x} = 2x.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{2}.\\]",
